The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit step did nothing: session_plan/ is gitignored, and the instruction's || true allows for that, so I didn't force-add it. The file is on disk for the planner.

What matters most this session: @yuanhao answered two of my open questions at 21:35Z, six minutes before this session started.

• #1055: he decided the outside-read fence stays on at a terminal. He asked me to drop "provisional" from the docs and release notes, then close the issue. The word is still in two places: CHANGELOG.md:20 and line 6 of the GitHub v0.3.0 release notes. docs/src has none. This is small and safe, and closing the issue and replying on Discussion #1048 should be named steps in the plan.
• #1064 (with #1067 merged in):
  • Key lookup: he wants yoyo to find API keys the way yoagent does (resolve_api_key / api_key_variables) instead of using its own one-variable-per-provider table.
  • Scrub default: he asked me to weigh removing keys by default for MCP servers and hooks, while the shell stays unchanged.
• The table problem is a real bug, and I reproduced it. With only GEMINI_API_KEY set and --provider google, yoyo says "No API key found" and exits 1. yoagent reads GEMINI_API_KEY before GOOGLE_API_KEY, but yoyo's table at src/providers.rs:23 only knows GOOGLE_API_KEY. The table has 27 callers outside tests, listed in the assessment but not yet sorted by what they do with it. #1062 (a key passed with --api-key is invisible to the setup wizard and the 401 hint) is the same problem.

Build and runs: a quick -p run of the binary worked. The last 4 evolve runs and the last 5 CI runs all succeeded, with no reverts in the window.

Research (saved to yopedia):
• Rivals: Claude Code and Codex both leave keys in child processes unless the user opts in. Claude Code's opt-in switch covers the shell, hooks and MCP servers; ours covers only the shell.
• MCP mechanism: yoagent's MCP launcher only adds environment variables and never removes any, so a default scrub for MCP servers needs another way in. One option is launching the server through env -u; the other is asking yoagent for an option. Hooks are easy because yoyo starts them itself (src/hooks.rs:741).

Also in the assessment:
• Three bugs I found by reading code, not by running it: #1063, #1045, #1057.
